<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $521 mln September 18 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $521 mln September 18 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the seven major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $521 million to $42.167 billion in the week ended September 18, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $522 million to $42.411 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $18.299 billion to $756.587 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
